{
  "name": "mixed-late-lock-head-replaced",
  "note": "LateIndexWrite on the mixed store (phase F part 10d, found by a random case of a 300 s make sim-campaign): lock client b (store ConditionalOverwrite, encrypted template) commits b1 under the lock; its plain head PUT of generation 3 is delayed and b1 fails Injected with no snapshot, releasing its lock. b2 takes the lock and reads head 2; the delayed PUT then lands (its lock violation, the late index write) and b2's plain PUT of generation 3 replaces it (HeadOverwritten at b2's own write). The replaced head named only the failed run's objects, so no committed snapshot loses coverage: H3's mechanism with no damage, the late write's trace. Claimed only when the replaced write is a lock client's released plain head PUT of a run that failed without a snapshot and the overwrite a lock client's plain PUT (tests::sim_driver::a_late_lock_head_replaced_by_a_lock_holder_is_a_late_index_write). Client a's delete runs first, lock-free. Not planned to close: the fallback's late-PUT limit.",
